# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in what you need. All keys are free.
# One source now requires a key; the rest work keyless at the volumes we pull.
# `ingest.common.read_secret` reads that copy, so no `export` is needed.
#
# THIS file is tracked, so every value below stays empty. Put the key in `.env`, never
# here. A pre-commit hook rejects this file if anything follows an `=`, because that has
# already happened once.

# data.cdc.gov Socrata app token — raises the anonymous rate limit on the
# CDC Alzheimer's & Healthy Aging bulk pull. https://evergreen.data.socrata.com/signup
SOCRATA_APP_TOKEN=

# BLS Public API v2 key — not needed. The flat files at download.bls.gov are the source of
# record, and the unkeyed API is called once per run only to cross-check the deflator's
# latest value. Unregistered callers get three years of history, which is plenty for that.
# Register only if the anonymous daily quota ever bites. https://data.bls.gov/registrationEngine/
BLS_API_KEY=

# api.census.gov key — REQUIRED. The API no longer serves unkeyed data requests: it
# answers them with an HTML page titled "Missing Key" and an HTTP 200 status, so a
# missing key looks like a parse error rather than an auth error. `just shared` fails
# with instructions if this is unset. Free, instant, no approval step.
# https://api.census.gov/data/key_signup.html
CENSUS_API_KEY=

# huduser.gov bearer token — REQUIRED for the ZIP-to-county crosswalk, which is what gives
# CFPB complaints a Michigan county grain (they publish state and ZIP only). Free: register,
# select the **USPS Crosswalk** dataset — not Fair Market Rents, Income Limits or CHAS, none
# of which any question here needs — confirm the email, then Create New Token. Unlike the
# Census key, a missing one fails honestly: HUD answers 401 with a JSON error body.
# https://www.huduser.gov/hudapi/public/login
HUD_API_TOKEN=
